    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαρτιχόρας</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>man-eater</i>, i.e.
			<i>tiger</i>, described with fabulous attributes by <i><span class="en">
				Ctes.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				501a26
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαρτιοχώρας, μαντιχώρας</span>
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ctes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				57.7
			</span></i>, Id. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				9.21.4
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαρτιόρα</span> codd.), et
				ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				4.21
			</span></i>. (Cf. Opers. <i>martiya</i>- 'man', Avest. <i>khwar</i>-
			'eat', Mod. <i><span class="en">
				Pers.
			</span></i>
			<i>mard-khwār</i> 'man-eater'.)</div>
